<h1>Optimise Scan</h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Scan Data &gt; Optimise Scan</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Optimise Scan</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command reduces the noise in scan data by aligning patches. Noise introduced by the arm, poor alignment, or synchronisation problems may lead to bad overlapping of the patches. Sometimes patches are detached each other at significant distance, sometimes they cross each other. Such scans later will produce poor meshes – areas with bad patch overlapping will be treated as features.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected scan data entities as well as on partial selection.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When you enter</span> <span class="Mode">Optimise</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode the scan becomes coloured as each patch has its own colour. When you see a clear colour at the patch boundaries, in most cases this means,</span> that the neighbouring patches are not well overlapped. When patches are overlapped, their colours are dithered each other.</p>
<p class="Example"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP235229049" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../transformation_menu/optimise.gif" width="349px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="parameterstitle">Optimise parameters:</p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../transformation_menu/optimise_mode.gif" width="223px" height="285px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Sample 1 in every</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Number of points to be skipped for processing. Increase the number if you don’t have enough memory. Default value is 1 point, i.e. every point will be used in optimisation process.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Maximum distance</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Limit of the patches offset from their original position. Default value is 1mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Number of iterations</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Number times the algorithm should be applied. Larger values increase the quality of the selected scan. Default value is 1.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Iteration method group</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Parallel</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">- Aligns patches simultaneously. This is the default method.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Sequential</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">- Aligns patches one after another.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP235633303" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table class="TableGrid" style="border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:5px;" cellspacing="5">
<tr valign="middle" class="whs6">
<td valign="top" class="whs7">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../transformation_menu/Commands_files/image399.gif" width="318px" height="180px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs7">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../transformation_menu/Commands_files/image400.gif" width="318px" height="180px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs6">
<td colspan="2" valign="top" class="whs7">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Patches in scan do not overlap (Smooth Shaded and Points render modes)</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs6">
<td valign="top" class="whs7">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../transformation_menu/Commands_files/image402.jpg" width="322px" height="183px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs7">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../transformation_menu/Commands_files/image404.jpg" width="322px" height="183px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs6">
<td colspan="2" valign="top" class="whs7">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Scan optimised – patches overlap (Smooth Shaded and Points render modes)</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
</div>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Optimise Scan</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to align patches in scan data before any other point processing – exporting, mesh generation, inspection, registration, etc.</span> <span class="Command">Optimise Scan</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is also used as internal algorithm in</span> <span class="Command">Merge</span> <span lang="EN-GB">and it is trying to resolve this problem by aligning patches. Another usage of this process is in</span> <u style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><b>Inspection</b></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">and</span> <u style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><b>Registration</b></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">facilities of KUBE.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">&#160;</p>
